              "text": "{\"problem\": {\"theorem\": \"Let $f$ be a continuous real function on a metric space $X$. Let $Z(f)$ (the zero set of $f$ ) be the set of all $p \\\\in X$ at which $f(p)=0$. Prove that $Z(f)$ is closed.\", \"assumptions\": [], \"domain\": \"real_analysis\", \"explicit_subgoals\": []}, \"candidate_text\": \"\\\\begin{proof}\\n\\n    $Z(f)=f^{-1}(\\\\{0\\\\})$, which is the inverse image of a closed set.\\n Hence $Z(f)$ is closed.\\n\\n\\\\end{proof}\", \"nodes\": [{\"node_id\": \"n1\", \"text\": \"\\\\begin{proof}\\n\\n    $Z(f)=f^{-1}(\\\\{0\\\\})$, which is the inverse image of a closed set.\"}, {\"node_id\": \"n2\", \"text\": \" Hence $Z(f)$ is closed.\\n\\n\\\\end{proof}\"}]}",
